  "verified_contract_facts": [
    "Instagram Login client_id/client_secret come from the Instagram product, not inferred from WhatsApp configuration.",
    "Authorization code exchange returns permissions and an app-scoped user reference; a separate /me user_id identifies the professional account and matches the webhook account identity. Keep id and user_id distinct.",
    "Short token can be exchanged for a long token; use returned expires_in. No permanent-token claim. Refresh prerequisites are separate from reauthorization.",
    "Instagram Login subscribes the professional account /subscribed_apps on graph.instagram.com; app-level field subscription and account-level subscription are both required.",
    "Message recipient is IGSID, send acceptance includes message_id. IN and echo have different sender/recipient orientation; mid is the message identity.",
    "Signed event timestamp qualifies policy; notification delivery time does not stand in for the original user action.",
    "Webhook documentation describes SHA256 signature with App Secret, raw payload verification and up to1000updates/batch. The chosen webhook secret must be configured explicitly for the app, separate from the OAuth-secret purpose.",
    "Most response windows are24h; click-to-Direct action may allow7days. LeadsHug first slice intentionally uses only a24hreply policy and no HumanAgent extension.",
    "Official get-started/webhook examples explicitly use Graph v26.0. Installation config still must set the version explicitly; test values do not imply a live grant."
  ],
